::ENG4_U01_L07_GP_Q1::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: Digital tools can expand learning when students use them with purpose. A note-taking application can help a student organize source ideas, and a shared document can make peer feedback more efficient. However, technology does not automatically improve learning. If students copy information without paraphrasing, accept suggestions without evaluating them, or use digital tools to avoid careful thinking, the tool weakens rather than strengthens academic work. Which paraphrase preserves the passage's qualification? {
~A. Technology always improves learning.#This ignores the qualification.
=B. Technology can support learning when students use it purposefully and keep thinking carefully.#Correct. This preserves the condition.
~C. Technology always weakens academic work.#This ignores the positive condition.
~D. Students should avoid all digital tools.#This distorts the passage.
}

::ENG4_U01_L07_GP_Q2::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: Responsible technology use requires students to preserve source meaning, evaluate support, and communicate conclusions clearly. What does preserve mean here? {
~A. Remove#This is the opposite.
~B. Decorate#This is unrelated.
~C. Guess quickly#This is unrelated.
=D. Keep accurately#Correct. Students must keep source meaning accurate.
}

::ENG4_U01_L07_GP_Q3::[MLA.ENG4.C.01] Passage: If students copy information without paraphrasing, accept suggestions without evaluating them, or use digital tools to avoid careful thinking, the tool weakens rather than strengthens academic work. Which oral explanation is most coherent? {
=A. The passage warns that tools can weaken work when students copy without paraphrasing or accept suggestions without evaluation.#Correct. This states the warning and evidence clearly.
~B. Technology is bad because apps and stuff.#This is vague.
~C. Digital tools are always efficient, so the passage supports them completely.#This ignores the warning.
~D. The passage has a lot of examples, so it is about examples.#This does not explain meaning.
}

::ENG4_U01_L07_GP_Q4::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: Responsible technology use requires students to preserve source meaning, evaluate support, and communicate conclusions clearly. Which sentence follows standard conventions? {
~A. Responsible technology use require students to preserve meaning.#The subject and verb do not agree.
~B. Responsible technology use requires students preserve meaning evaluate support and communicate clearly.#Commas are needed for clarity in the series.
=C. Responsible technology use requires students to preserve meaning, evaluate support, and communicate clearly.#Correct. The series is clear and grammatical.
~D. responsible technology use requires students to preserve meaning.#The sentence begins with a lowercase letter.
}

::ENG4_U01_L07_GP_Q5::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: A note-taking application can help a student organize source ideas, and a shared document can make peer feedback more efficient. However, technology does not automatically improve learning. Which claim is best supported? {
~A. Digital tools are useless in academic work.#This contradicts the positive examples.
=B. Digital tools are helpful only when used purposefully.#Correct. This preserves the passage's balanced view.
~C. Shared documents prevent all feedback problems.#This overstates the source.
~D. Note-taking applications replace careful reading.#This is unsupported.
}
